{title: Hallelujah! What a Saviour}
{artist: Philip P. Bliss}
{genre: Easter, Gospel}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Man of Sorrows, [Bb]what a name
[F]For the Son of [C]God, who came
[F]Ruined sinners [Bb]to reclaim
[F]Hallelujah, [C]what a Sa[F]viour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Bearing shame and [Bb]scoffing rude
[F]In my place con[C]demned He stood
[F]Sealed my pardon [Bb]with His blood
[F]Hallelujah, [C]what a Sa[F]viour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Guilty, vile, and [Bb]helpless we
[F]Spotless Lamb of [C]God was He
[F]Full atonement, [Bb]can it be
[F]Hallelujah, [C]what a Sa[F]viour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Lifted up was [Bb]He to die
[F]It is finished, [C]was His cry
[F]Now in heaven [Bb]exalted high
[F]Hallelujah, [C]what a Sa[F]viour
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]When He comes, our [Bb]glorious King
[F]All His ransomed [C]home to bring
[F]Then anew this [Bb]song we'll sing
[F]Hallelujah, [C]what a Sa[F]viour
{end_of_verse}
